  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-04-27T12:41:09.924Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Link to the full document: https://docs.google.com/document/d/15FHx4zegeACWjPiPEbSta3WZkIXiHAZjXXCxL-9rPak/edit\nI have recently sent in a support email concerning this, as I did not feel as though the Canny was the best spot for it. However, I was redirected to here anyway, and thus I will leave it here for consideration by the VRChat leadership.\nThe link delves more in-depth, but in short, I believe it to be a necessary and healthy thing for VRChat to bring on a team of vetted volunteers who can provide for limited but effective in-game moderation, as opposed to the once-all-is-done faceless unknown ticket system where we have no idea if anything even happened.\nIf VRChat is going to keep growing, and to be a safe place for legal players and to be a community *of* legal players, then there needs to be effective in-game moderation to keep the peace, not to let it be an absolute wasteland/anarchy with solely a ticket system that has no face, no apparent resolution, or anything. Issues pop up that require immediate action, and in some cases Vigilante-crashers have arisen to fill that gap in, by doing wrong to try to bring about a positive.\nIf any other players who read this have input they would like to give, be it with other issues they have noticed, thoughts on such a pseudo-moderation force, or otherwise, please drop a comment.",
